# hypre Interface Tests

This directory builds the hypre `ij` driver with the ParGeMSLR preconditioner registered as solver option 83. The tested bundled hypre baseline is v3.1.0 from `ParGeMSLR/external/hypre`.

The repository CMake build can compile the pinned hypre source, adapter, and
`ij` driver together with `PARGEMSLR_ENABLE_HYPRE=ON`. It registers strict
host tests at one and two MPI ranks; CUDA builds also register matching device
tests. See [`BUILDING.md`](../../../BUILDING.md) for bundled and system-provider
commands.

## Build hypre

From `ParGeMSLR`, build the bundled CPU hypre:

```bash
bash buildhypre.sh cpu
```

For a bundled CUDA hypre build, use:

```bash
CUDA_ARCH=86 bash buildhypre.sh cuda
```

`HYPRE_UNIFIED_MEMORY=1` and `HYPRE_GPU_AWARE_MPI=1` can be added to the CUDA build command when those modes are required by the target system. The bundled CUDA build defaults to `--without-umpire`; set `HYPRE_WITH_UMPIRE=1` plus `HYPRE_UMPIRE_INCLUDE`, `HYPRE_UMPIRE_LIB_DIRS`, and `HYPRE_UMPIRE_LIBS` to use a system Umpire install.

## CPU Build and Checks

Build ParGeMSLR first, then build this test driver:

```bash
cd ParGeMSLR
make
cd TESTS/hypre
make
```

To use a system or module-provided hypre build, pass a configured hypre build directory while building the driver. Relative `HYPRE_PATH` values are interpreted from the `ParGeMSLR` directory; absolute paths are also accepted.

```bash
cd ParGeMSLR/TESTS/hypre
make HYPRE_PATH=/path/to/hypre/build
```

Basic CPU checks:

```bash
mpirun -np 1 ./ij -solver 83 -n 8 8 8 -shift 0.5 -k 50 -exec_host
mpirun -np 2 ./ij -solver 83 -n 8 8 8 -shift 0.5 -k 50 -exec_host
```

## CUDA Build and Checks

Build both ParGeMSLR and this driver with CUDA enabled:

```bash
cd ParGeMSLR
make USING_CUDA=1 CUDA_VERSION=12 CUDA_ARCH=86
cd TESTS/hypre
make USING_CUDA=1 CUDA_VERSION=12
```

When `USING_CUDA=1` and `HYPRE_PATH` is not set, this test Makefile selects `external/hypre-build/cuda/src`. Set `HYPRE_PATH=/path/to/cuda/hypre/build` while building the driver to use a system CUDA hypre build.

CUDA checks:

```bash
mpirun -np 1 ./ij -solver 83 -n 8 8 8 -shift 0.5 -k 50 -exec_device
mpirun -np 2 ./ij -solver 83 -n 8 8 8 -shift 0.5 -k 50 -exec_device
```

Use the reported `Final FlexGMRES Relative Residual Norm` and iteration count to compare CPU, MPI rank counts, and CUDA runs.
